    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0477" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/277</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé d’Affaires in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-07T14:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 7, 1914, 2 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Your telegram of August 6, 8 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d287-f1"/> Report
                    nationality and numbers of troops withdrawn from the railway and of those
                    remaining. Has the Diplomatic Corps recently discussed question of continuing
                    railway guards? Have governments withdrawing made any arrangements with other
                    powers for substitutes?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
